        "Hoa Tien Cave lies in the area of Suoi Hoa (the Ngoi Hoa region), former Tan Lac district (now Phu Tho), within Ngoi Hoa Bay — one of the loveliest parts of Hoa Binh Lake. It is a large limestone cave inside the mountain, likened to a 'fairyland' with a spacious interior, high ceiling and several connected chambers. Inside are rich stalactites, stalagmites and columns in strange shapes, glittering in many colours under the light and evoking natural and spiritual images. Locals link the cave to Mother Goddess worship, setting up an altar within, so it combines natural beauty with a sacred air. To reach Hoa Tien Cave, visitors usually travel by boat on Hoa Binh Lake, admiring Ngoi Hoa Bay with its blue water, ranks of mountains and lakeside hamlets, and may swim, fish and enjoy Da River specialities. Still fairly new and wild, Hoa Tien Cave suits those who love exploration and untouched nature. As land and water access here remains limited, visitors should ask locals carefully and hire a boat and guide for a smooth, safe trip.",
